Subject: [PATCH 148/260] [ae-patch] Cache the gh auth status answer for 60
 seconds across the host's processes

Every read of a session's GitHub resource ran gh auth status --json hosts, in
the session's runner or the host service. The merge watcher reads every recent
session each 120 seconds, so a box with a dozen sessions ran several of these
per burst, all in the same second (39 of 135 gh processes in ten minutes).

_list_accounts now goes through omnigent/runner/_ae_gh_auth_cache.py: one small
file per user under the cache dir, keyed by the gh config dir, hosts.yml size and
mtime, the sandbox flag and a hash of the GH token variables. Only an
authenticated answer is cached; a failed gh call with an authentication error
drops the entry, and concurrent misses share one gh run through a file lock.
OMNIGENT_GH_AUTH_CACHE_SECONDS sets the TTL (0 turns it off); the root test
conftest turns it off so stubbed gh answers never leak between tests.
